  "question": {
    "text": "The atomic number of Unnilumium is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "101",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to IUPAC convention for naming of elements with atomic number more than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>, different digits are written in order and at the end ium is added. For digits following naming is used.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>nil</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>un</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>bi</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>tri</mi></math></p><p>and so on...</p>",
